__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# training artefacts: policies are outputs, not source
runs/
*.zip
*.pt
*.pth

# TacView recordings
*.acmi

# Screen captures.  The raw grab is an intermediate -- a 25 s desktop
# recording is 175 MB, which GitHub refuses outright at 100 MB.  What ships
# is the GIF made from it, which lives next to the README that shows it.
*.mkv
*.mp4
!**/docs/*.gif

# The answer key.  A student repo is downstream of this one, so once this lands
# in history it cannot be taken back out.  Moves to a private submodule later.
# solutions/

# Superseded work, kept on disk for reference only -- old checkpoints, runs
# whose spec has since changed, results that today's code cannot even load.
# Hundreds of MB of that does not belong in anyone's clone.
#
# No leading slash, so this matches an `archived/` directory at ANY depth:
# `archived/` at the root, `solutions/project_01_circular/archived/`, and any
# that appear later.  The convention is one `archived/` per folder that needs
# one, rather than one central graveyard -- superseded results stay next to the
# code that produced them, which is where anyone looking for them will be.
archived/
